  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an integer NNN. You have to find a permutation PPP of the integers {1,2,…,N}\\{1, 2, \\ldots, N\\}{1,2,…,N} that satisfies MMM conditions of the following form:\n\n\n(Xi,Yi)(X_i, Y_i)(Xi​,Yi​), denoting that the element Xi  (1≤Xi≤N)X_i\\;(1\\leq X_i \\leq N)Xi​(1≤Xi​≤N) must appear in the prefix of length YiY_iYi​. Formally, if the index of the element XiX_iXi​ is KiK_iKi​ (i.e, PKi=XiP_{K_i} = X_iPKi​​=Xi​), then the condition 1≤Ki≤Yi1\\le K_i \\le Y_i1≤Ki​≤Yi​ must hold.\nPrint `-1` if no such permutation exists. In case multiple permutations that satisfy all the conditions exist, find the **lexicographically smallest** one.\n\n**Note:** If two arrays AAA and BBB have the same length NNN, then AAA is called lexicographically smaller than BBB only if there exists an index i  (1≤i≤N)i \\; (1\\leq i \\leq N)i(1≤i≤N) such that A1=B1,A_1=B_1,A1​=B1​, A2=B2,A_2=B_2,A2​=B2​, …,\\ldots,…, Ai−1=Bi−1,Ai&lt;BiA_{i-1}=B_{i-1}, A_i \\lt B_iAi−1​=Bi−1​,Ai​&lt;Bi​.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and MMM — the length of permutation and the number of conditions to be satisfied respectively.\nThe next MMM lines describe the conditions. The iii-th of these MMM lines contains two space-separated integers XiX_iXi​ and YiY_iYi​.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output a single line containing the answer:\n\n\n\nIf no permutation satisfies the given conditions, print `−1`.\nOtherwise, print NNN space-separated integers, denoting the elements of the permutation. If there are multiple answers, output the lexicographically smallest one.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤M≤N1 \\leq M \\leq N1≤M≤N",
      "1≤Xi,Yi≤N1 \\leq X_i, Y_i \\leq N1≤Xi​,Yi​≤N",
      "Xi≠XjX_i \\neq X_jXi​=Xj​ for each 1≤i&lt;j≤M1 \\leq i \\lt j \\leq M1≤i&lt;j≤M.",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
